# V1 getting started

<!-- Generated by scripts/generate-v1-guides.ts from executed canonical source. Do not edit this output by hand. -->

Fadeno V1 is a working experimental framework. This guide targets the first
public alpha registry release source, `@fadeno/framework@0.1.0-alpha.1`, and uses the
[canonical packed application](../../examples/v1-app/README.md), whose check,
build, development, production start, routes, failures, and recovery are
executed by the local merge gate.

## Requirements and current boundary

Use Node.js 22.17 or newer and the repository's locked package manager. From a
clean checkout, install with `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`. The selected
registry version is `@fadeno/framework@0.1.0-alpha.1`; registry availability and
provenance are accepted only when `pnpm verify:a0-public-alpha` passes. The
project-creation and deployment commands exist in reviewed packed artifacts.
This experimental alpha has no production-support or stable-compatibility
promise.

## Create a project

The installed `@fadeno/framework` package exposes one exact non-interactive
command. Its parent path must already exist without requested symlink
components, and the target must not exist:

```sh
fadeno create --project-root ./my-fadeno-app
```

The normalized success output below is captured from the current packed
package. The generated manifest is compared byte-for-byte with the actual
created project before dependencies or build output exist.

